  "reading": "56 starts across four titles, 14 per title, every one of them a byte-identical tail of a full decode -- which is also the proof that every landing access unit really carries a major sync, since a unit without restart headers would begin from zero filter history and could not reproduce the tail. The worst snap forward was 126, 123, 127 and 122 access units (about 105 ms), bounded by the 128-unit max_major_sync_interval each stream reports, but the landing points are not on a 128 grid: pi-head50m carries a major sync at unit 1 and shaun-head20m at unit 18, because a cut clip's sync points are irregular. This refuted the sentence first committed in docs/truehd.md, which asserted 128 access units without measuring."
}